#: ../../reference/cli.rst:264
msgid "The build prints what it read and wrote, then a verdict: ``build succeeded`` or ``build failed``, with the number of errors and warnings and where the output is. A failed build leaves the previous output as it was. The warnings of ``conf.toml`` are the build's own, so ``-W`` counts them. ``suppress_warnings`` silences warnings before ``-W`` counts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/cli.rst:269
msgid "``read`` counts the documents parsed and those unchanged since the last build (taken from the environment). ``write`` counts the outputs written and those kept. An output is a page for ``html``, ``dirhtml`` and ``text`` (and the search index in the HTML builders), a book for ``pdf``, and the single output of ``singlehtml`` and ``gettext``. Every build also writes the site's shared files (theme, indexes, ``objects.inv``). They are not counted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/cli.rst:276
msgid "guidedog serve"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/cli.rst:279
msgid "Builds the HTML site and serves it on ``http://127.0.0.1:PORT/``. When sources, templates, static files, or ``conf.toml`` changed, it rebuilds before answering a request:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/cli.rst:287
msgid "``--port PORT`` (``-p`` is quickstart's project name, not the port) chooses the port, from 1 to 65535 (default: ``8000``). ``-c``, ``-C``, ``-D name=value`` and the build options of ``guidedog build`` apply to every rebuild. Each rebuild reloads ``conf.toml``. A failed rebuild keeps the previous site and reports the problem. Ctrl+C stops the server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/cli.rst:292
msgid "It serves ``_build/html``. It watches the source folder, the Odin and Rust API sources (``odin_autoapi_dirs``, ``odin_collections``, ``rust_autoapi_crates``), and the ``html_static_path``, ``html_extra_path``, ``templates_path``, ``include_roots``, ``autodoc_source_paths`` and ``locale_dirs`` folders outside the source folder. The build folder is never watched. Changes are found by file names, sizes and times. The check runs before an HTML page is answered:"
msgstr ""

