msgid "A timeout or Ctrl+C after a possible write reports an unknown outcome (exit status 7). We then run the publisher's recovery command before retrying. Each invocation builds into its own private folder, which is removed afterwards. Concurrent invocations cannot change each other's snapshots. See :doc:`../plugins`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/cli.rst:572
msgid "guidedog publish pages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/cli.rst:575
msgid "``guidedog publish pages`` is the guided way to GitHub Pages; the GitHub Pages plugin adds it. It does whatever is still missing and asks only when it must. Then it builds and publishes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/cli.rst:578
msgid "``pages.toml``: written once, with the repository taken from the ``origin`` remote and the project from the nearest ``conf.toml`` (or as given)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/cli.rst:580
msgid "A token: GitHub's device sign-in, stored in the system's credential store, or the GitHub CLI's token for this run only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/cli.rst:582
msgid "The binding: the target is reviewed, and it asks us once to let this machine publish there."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/cli.rst:584
msgid "The Pages source: when Pages publishes another branch, or uses Actions, it asks us once to switch it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/cli.rst:586
msgid "The publication: one push to the site's own branch, then a wait for the deployment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/cli.rst:588
msgid "On a machine that is already set up, it publishes without a question. Without a terminal it never asks. A missing step then fails with a hint naming the command or option that does it. ``--yes`` answers the confirmations. It never signs in or replaces other work on our behalf. Its options are those of ``guidedog-pages init`` and ``publish`` (``--config``, ``--repository``, ``--project``, ``--branch``, ``--profile``, ``--wait``, ``--verbose``, ``--dry-run``); ``guidedog publish pages --help`` lists them. guidedog builds the project itself, with its own engine and linked plugins; ``--guidedog=PATH`` builds with another program instead. See :doc:`../howto/github-pages`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/cli.rst:596
msgid "guidedog pages workflow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/cli.rst:599
msgid "``guidedog pages workflow`` is ``guidedog-pages workflow``, added by the GitHub Pages plugin. It prints, writes, or checks a GitHub Actions workflow. The workflow installs this Guidedog release, builds the project, and deploys it with GitHub's Pages actions. We use it instead of publishing from our own machine when every push to the source branch should deploy."
msgstr ""

