#: ../../reference/configuration.rst:1
msgid "Configuration reference"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/configuration.rst:4
msgid "Every Guidedog documentation project is configured with ``conf.toml``. Guidedog reads it as TOML data and runs no code. Setting names are those of Sphinx's ``conf.py``. So ``guidedog migrate conf.py`` can translate an existing project, and the Sphinx documentation describes the settings Guidedog shares with it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/configuration.rst:9
msgid "This page lists every setting Guidedog reads. The settings are flat top-level keys, as in ``conf.py``. A table setting is written as a TOML table (``[html_context]``) or an inline table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/configuration.rst:13
msgid "Where conf.toml is"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/configuration.rst:16
msgid "Guidedog looks for ``conf.toml`` in the project folder, then in ``PROJECT/source`` (the separated layout of ``quickstart --sep``, with ``build/`` beside ``source/``), then in the nearest parent folder that has one. The folder holding ``conf.toml`` is the source folder. The build folder is ``_build`` beside it, or ``build`` in the separated layout. ``guidedog build -c DIR`` reads ``conf.toml`` from another folder. ``-C`` builds without one, with the defaults below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/configuration.rst:23
msgid "``-D name=value`` overrides one setting for one build. The value is TOML (``-D numfig=true``, ``-D 'exclude_patterns=[\"drafts/**\"]'``). A bare word is read as a string (``-D language=de``). ``-D html_context.key=value`` sets one key of a table setting and keeps the others, as sphinx-build does."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/configuration.rst:28
msgid "Minimal configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/configuration.rst:31
msgid "A project needs only basic metadata. Omitted keys take their defaults:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/configuration.rst:46
msgid "How settings are checked"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/configuration.rst:49
msgid "Each value is checked against its type when ``conf.toml`` is read. A mistake is an ``INVALID CONFIGURATION`` problem (exit status 2) naming the line and the expected form. An unknown setting is an error too, with a \"Did you mean ...?\" hint when the name is close to a known one. A setting of a Sphinx builder or extension Guidedog does not have (``latex_*``, ``epub_*``, ``man_*``, ``texinfo_*``, ``doctest_*``, ``linkcheck_*``, ``html_sidebars``, ``needs_*`` and similar) is accepted with a ``config.ignored`` warning. So the same file can serve a Sphinx build of the sources."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/configuration.rst:57
msgid "Some values are derived after reading:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/configuration.rst:59
msgid "``release`` defaults to ``version``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/configuration.rst:60
msgid "``html_title`` defaults to ``\"<project> <release> documentation\"`` (or ``\"<project> documentation\"`` without a release). ``html_short_title`` defaults to ``html_title``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/configuration.rst:63
msgid "Without ``pdf_documents``, the project has one book. It starts from ``root_doc``, is titled with ``project``, is by ``author``, and is in a file named after the project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/configuration.rst:65
msgid "``extensions = [\"myst_parser\"]`` adds ``.md`` to ``source_suffix``, as the Sphinx extension does."
